        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be fixed on latest `main`. All 'mini.nvim' modules that can open file for an edit now mimic the behavior of `:edit` as described in `:h buffer-reuse`. It is not *exactly* the same, as buffer is not get reused, but user-facing outcome is the same: the current empty-unnamed-unmodified-singleview will be replaced with the buffer for a file.\n\nThanks again for noticing this!",
